---
/**
 * The method in four layers that the page keeps apart: what depends on
 * what, what time it is read against, what evidence it needs, and how the
 * conclusion is formed. The three verdict states themselves are listed once
 * on this page, under the chain, and shown on the AGDA® page; they are not
 * drawn again here. An executive reading of the page; each layer links to the
 * section that carries the detail.
 *
 * The statements are the methodology page's own. The marks are diagrams of
 * those statements, not data: nothing here is a score, a measurement or a
 * result. The four evidence kinds are drawn in the order the page's own
 * evidence ladder gives them.
 */
---
<figure class="method-layers" aria-label="The method in four layers">
  <ol role="list">
    <li>
      <h3>Operational dependencies</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 260 44" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <line x1="8" y1="14" x2="252" y2="14" />
        {[8, 89, 171, 252].map((x) => <circle cx={x} cy="14" r="6.5" />)}
        {['Detect', 'Escalate', 'Decide', 'Intervene'].map((t, i) => <text x={[2, 89, 171, 258][i]} y="40" text-anchor={i === 0 ? 'start' : i === 3 ? 'end' : 'middle'}>{t}</text>)}
      </svg>
      <p>Detect, Escalate, Decide, Intervene. Four sequential stages. A downstream stage depends on what reaches it.</p>
      <a href="#chain">The chain <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Timing</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 260 44" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect class="ml-track" x="2" y="8" width="256" height="12" />
        <rect class="ml-fill" x="2" y="8" width="150" height="12" />
        <line class="ml-edge" x1="206" y1="0" x2="206" y2="28" />
        <text x="2" y="40">Chain</text>
        <text class="ml-edge-text" x="206" y="40" text-anchor="middle">Available time</text>
      </svg>
      <p>The stages run against the available time, which is set in scope. The engine computes whether the cumulative chain completes before harm becomes irreversible.</p>
      <a href="#scope">Scope first <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Evidence</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 260 44" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        {[9, 15, 21, 27].map((h, i) => <rect class="ml-fill" x={2 + i * 66} y={28 - h} width="58" height={h} />)}
        {['Policy', 'Drill', 'Production', 'Stress'].map((t, i) => <text x={2 + i * 66} y="40">{t}</text>)}
      </svg>
      <p>Policy, drill, production and stress evidence carry different weight. Confidence cannot outrun the evidence.</p>
      <a href="#evidence">Evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Judgement</h3>
      {/* The first label is set on two lines beneath its own marker, so it stays clear of the middle one. */}
      <svg viewBox="0 0 260 55" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <line x1="16" y1="14" x2="244" y2="14" />
        <rect class="ml-fill" x="2" y="7" width="14" height="14" />
        <circle cx="130" cy="14" r="7" />
        <rect class="ml-box" x="244" y="7" width="14" height="14" />
        <text x="2" y="40"><tspan x="2">Engine</tspan><tspan x="2" dy="12">computation</tspan></text>
        {['Interpretation', 'Conclusion'].map((t, i) => <text x={[130, 258][i]} y="40" text-anchor={['middle', 'end'][i]}>{t}</text>)}
      </svg>
      <p>Repeatable engine computation supports the assessment. Intervene remains responsible for evidence interpretation and the final conclusion.</p>
      <a href="#chain">The three states <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>Diagrams of the method, not measurements. The underlying rubric and protected implementation remain Intervene IP.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .method-layers { margin: var(--gap-intro) 0 0; }
  ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); }
  li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr) auto; gap: var(--space-3) var(--space-6); align-items: center; padding: var(--space-5) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); }
  li:first-child { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  h3 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.2vw, 32px); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-heading); line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); }
  p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--type-body); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
  a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; min-height: 44px; white-space: nowrap; font-size: var(--type-action); font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--hair-strong); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  a:is(:hover, :focus-visible) { color: var(--accent-text); }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 340px; height: auto; overflow: visible; }
  svg line { stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1; }
  svg circle { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1; }
  svg text { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 9.5px; fill: var(--muted); }
  svg .ml-track { fill: var(--hair); }
  svg .ml-fill { fill: var(--ink); stroke: none; }
  svg .ml-edge { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2.5; }
  svg .ml-edge-text { fill: var(--accent-text); }
  svg .ml-box { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 2; }
  figcaption { margin-top: var(--space-3); font-size: var(--type-small); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    li { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr); }
    li > h3 { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
    li > svg { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 2; }
    li > p { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / 3; }
    li > a { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 3; justify-self: start; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    li { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); padding: var(--space-4) 0; }
    li > :is(h3, svg, p, a) { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
  }
</style>
